tus="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MITSUBISHI DENKI KABUSHIKI KAISHA</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HAZAMA KAORI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HAZAMA, KAORI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>When a mobile communication device detects a communication line in a satisfactory line state, the identification information of a system side communication device providing the communication line is extracted and stored in relation to the communication line. In order to switch the line, a stored communication line whose identification information agrees with the identification information of a communication line being captured is selected preferentially to finish the line search in a short time.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Lorsqu'un dispositif de communication mobile détecte une ligne de communication dont les conditions sont satisfaisantes, l'information d'identification d'un dispositif système de communication est extraite et stockée pour ladite ligne de communication. Pour commuter la ligne, et pour que la recherche de ligne soit menée à bien rapidement, on sélectionne une ligne de communication stockée dont l'information d'identification est conforme avec l'information d'identification d'une ligne de communication en passe d'être retenue.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreem